MODERN ISA-POL PRESET DECLARATION TEXT / SOURCE NOTICES

isapol_modern_preset.py records, verbatim and line by line, the contents of
two CamCASP method templates and their cluster templates:

    methods/isa-pol-from-isa-A        methods/isa-pol-from-isa-A.clt_tmpl
    methods/isa-pol-from-isa-A+DF     methods/isa-pol-from-isa-A+DF.clt_tmpl

at CamCASP revision 63b16a22b9bae597fe81ecdb8b8d91c21868c814. The sha256 of
each file is pinned in the module (SOURCE_SHA256) and checked against the
reference tree by tests/pytests/test_isapol_modern_preset.py when that tree is
present, so a stale transcription is detectable rather than silent.

What is reproduced here is CamCASP keyword/declaration text -- the input
protocol -- together with this branch's statement of which declarations it
honours, which it provably cannot change under the same preset, and which it
does not honour at all (isapol_modern_preset.GAPS). No CamCASP algorithm,
source code or numerical result is reproduced in this module: it contains no
computation, reads no files and imports nothing from psi4.core.

The module emits no option for an unhonourable declaration, and its A+DF
manifest refuses to emit options at all, because ISA-A and ISA-A+DF are
different partitions and substituting one for the other would misstate which
model produced a number.

CamCASP permitted source-derived declaration provenance: Anthony Stone /
Alston Misquitta. The applicable notice retained from the owned CamCASP
fixture is reproduced in full below. It is not a license assertion about
ORIENT, RRF, or third-party basis databases; the basis names appearing in the
declaration text (aVTZ, Type MC, ISA-set2) are names only, and no basis data
is reproduced here -- see isapol_reference_basis.NOTICE for that.

